course: dictionary
lesson: 6490
title: Neanderthal: an early human, and a rude word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Neanderthal was a kind of early human who lived in Europe and western Asia, and then died out. «Neanderthals made tools, used fire, buried their dead and maybe made art.» Tools, fire and burial show they were clever and cared for each other, so you can see they were more than just brutes.
explain: Notice the small letter in «neanderthal» when someone uses it as an insult. Calling someone a neanderthal is informal and rude. It means they are rough, rude or old-fashioned in their ideas. Do not use it to hurt people, and use context to tell which meaning is being used.
explain: «Neanderthals were close human relatives who died out long ago.» The word relatives tells you they were family to us, not strangers. Scientists have read DNA from their old bones, and many people today carry a small part of it. This is how we know they were close to us.
fact: A Neanderthal was an early human who lived in Europe and western Asia.
fact: Neanderthals lived from about 400,000 to about 40,000 years ago, and then died out.
fact: Neanderthals made stone tools, used fire, wore clothes and buried their dead.
fact: The old idea that Neanderthals were stupid brutes is a myth: «their brains were as big as ours».
fact: Calling someone a «neanderthal» is informal and rude, and means rough, rude or old-fashioned.
exercise: «Neanderthals made tools, used fire, buried their dead and maybe made art.» Which of these did Neanderthals do? | Flew to the Moon | Wrote printed books | *Used fire | Built steam trains
exercise: Where did Neanderthals live? | Antarctica | Australia and South America | *Europe and western Asia | Only on islands in the Pacific
exercise: «Neanderthals were close human relatives who died out long ago.» What does «died out» mean? | Got lost in the woods | *Became extinct, and no longer lived anywhere | Went outside to play | Became famous
test: «Many people today carry a small part of Neanderthal DNA.» What does this tell us? | Neanderthal DNA is a kind of food | *Some people alive today have Neanderthal ancestors | Only animals have DNA | Neanderthals still live in Europe
test: Why is calling someone a neanderthal unkind? | *It means they are rough, rude or old-fashioned | It means they are a famous scientist | It means they are very clever | It means they are a kind friend
exam: In which year did Svante Pääbo win a Nobel Prize for work on Neanderthal DNA? | 2012 | 2002 | *2022 | 1922
